        ":question/id": "0eebeabb-6f2b-5bd5-8ffc-c7e26262f1dc",
        ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=1 - \\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}$ at $\\left(4,\\frac{1}{4}\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $y=ax+b$.\n\n$a=$ {{slope}}\n\n$b=$ {{intercept}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=1 - \\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}$. Rewrite with powers, then differentiate term by term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=(-1x^{- \\frac{1}{2}})+(-1x^{-1})+(1)\\\\\nf'(x)&=\\frac{1}{x^{2}} + \\frac{1}{2 x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(4\\right)=\\frac{1}{\\left(4\\right)^{2}} + \\frac{1}{2 \\left(4\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}=\\frac{1}{8}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)}=-8.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)&=-8\\left(x-\\left(4\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=- 8 x+\\left(32\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{129}{4} - 8 x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $a=-8$ and $b=\\frac{129}{4}$."
      }
