        ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=-1 - \\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{2}{x^{2}}$ at $\\left(2,- \\frac{5}{2}\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $y=ax+b$.\n\n$a=$ {{slope}}\n\n$b=$ {{intercept}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=-1 - \\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{2}{x^{2}}$. Rewrite with powers, then differentiate term by term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=(-2x^{-1})+(-2x^{-2})+(-1)\\\\\nf'(x)&=\\frac{2}{x^{2}} + \\frac{4}{x^{3}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(2\\right)=\\frac{2}{\\left(2\\right)^{2}} + \\frac{4}{\\left(2\\right)^{3}}=1\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(1\\right)}=-1.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(- \\frac{5}{2}\\right)&=-1\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=- x+\\left(2\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\\\\ny&=- x - \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $a=-1$ and $b=- \\frac{1}{2}$."
      }
